      ],
      "Deliverable Description": "A QA test plan lays out how a team will check that a product works before it ships: what will be tested, how, and what counts as passing. It is the roadmap for quality checking.",
      "Why Is This Deliverable Important?": "A clear plan means testing is thorough and repeatable instead of a scramble at the end, which protects users from broken releases.",
      "How Does This Deliverable Relate to Other Deliverables?": "It builds on requirements and acceptance criteria, spins off into detailed test cases, and drives the acceptance testing milestone.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "MDN Web Docs, a trusted resource for building software: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn"
    },
