      ],
      "Deliverable Description": "A task flow maps the steps a user takes to complete a single task, from start to finish. It shows the path through a product one goal at a time.",
      "Why Is This Deliverable Important?": "Laying out the steps reveals confusing detours and missing pieces early, so the team can smooth the path before building it.",
      "How Does This Deliverable Relate to Other Deliverables?": "Task flows come together in Requirements, lean on user stories and acceptance criteria, and guide the wireframes and prototypes designers create.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Agile Coach, with guides on agile, Scrum, and Kanban: https://www.atlassian.com/agile"
    },
