      ],
      "Deliverable Description": "A use case diagram is a simple picture showing who uses a product and the main things they can do with it. It gives a quick, big-picture view of the product's functions.",
      "Why Is This Deliverable Important?": "It helps everyone see the full set of interactions at a glance, which makes gaps and overlaps easy to catch early.",
      "How Does This Deliverable Relate to Other Deliverables?": "It comes from the Requirements milestone and summarizes the use case scenarios and user stories into one clear overview.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Agile Coach, with guides on agile, Scrum, and Kanban: https://www.atlassian.com/agile"
    },
