          "id": "spf:ux-user-experience-writing",
          "label": "UX (User Experience) Writing"
        }
      ],
      "Deliverable Description": "An editorial style guide is the rulebook for how a product's words sound, covering tone, wording, and formatting. It keeps the writing consistent no matter who is writing it.",
      "Why Is This Deliverable Important?": "Consistent, clear language makes a product feel trustworthy and easy to use, and it saves writers from reinventing the rules each time.",
      "How Does This Deliverable Relate to Other Deliverables?": "It is built in the Implement milestone alongside brand identity, and it guides the copywriting, microcopy, and content the team produces.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Nielsen Norman Group, a trusted source for UX research and design: https://www.nngroup.com/",
      "Hand-Off Deliverables Map": [
        {
          "id": "spf:part-3-the-outcomes",
          "label": "Part 3: The outcomes"
        }
      ]
