      ],
      "Deliverable Description": "A burn down chart shows how much work is left in a sprint as the days tick by. The line ideally drops toward zero by the sprint's end.",
      "Why Is This Deliverable Important?": "It gives the team a quick, honest read on whether they are on pace, so they can adjust before the sprint runs out.",
      "How Does This Deliverable Relate to Other Deliverables?": "Used across all milestones during sprints, it draws on the sprint plan and goals and feeds retrospective conversations.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Agile Coach, with guides on agile, Scrum, and Kanban: https://www.atlassian.com/agile"
    },
