      ],
      "Deliverable Description": "A refined backlog is a backlog that has been cleaned up and clarified, with items sized, detailed, and re-ordered. Refinement keeps the to-do list ready to work from.",
      "Why Is This Deliverable Important?": "A tidy backlog means sprint planning goes smoothly and the team is never left guessing what an item really means.",
      "How Does This Deliverable Relate to Other Deliverables?": "It evolves through Discovery and Requirements, building on the prioritized backlog and feeding the sprint plan every cycle.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Agile Coach, with guides on agile, Scrum, and Kanban: https://www.atlassian.com/agile",
      "Hand-Off Deliverables Map": [
        {
          "id": "spf:part-4-the-sequel",
