      "Deliverable Description": "A sprint plan is the team's agreement on what they will tackle in the next short work cycle. It picks a focused slice of the backlog to complete.",
      "Why Is This Deliverable Important?": "It gives the team a clear, achievable target for the sprint, which keeps agile work steady and predictable.",
      "How Does This Deliverable Relate to Other Deliverables?": "Made from the refined backlog and sprint goals, it drives the burn down chart and the demo and retro that close the sprint.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Agile Coach, with guides on agile, Scrum, and Kanban: https://www.atlassian.com/agile"
    },
