        }
      ],
      "Deliverable Description": "Wireframes are simple, low-detail sketches of a screen's layout, showing where things go without color or polish. They focus on structure, not looks.",
      "Why Is This Deliverable Important?": "Starting rough lets a team test and change ideas cheaply, before anyone invests in a finished-looking design.",
      "How Does This Deliverable Relate to Other Deliverables?": "Created in the Implement milestone from task flows and requirements, they are the first step toward low- and high-fidelity prototypes.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Nielsen Norman Group, a trusted source for UX research and design: https://www.nngroup.com/",
      "Hand-Off Deliverables Map": [
        {
          "id": "spf:part-3-the-outcomes",
          "label": "Part 3: The outcomes"
        }
      ]
    },
