      ],
      "Deliverable Description": "A low-fidelity prototype is a rough, clickable version of a product used to test ideas quickly. It is more interactive than a wireframe but far from finished.",
      "Why Is This Deliverable Important?": "It lets a team put a rough experience in front of people early and learn from real reactions before building the real thing.",
      "How Does This Deliverable Relate to Other Deliverables?": "Built in Implement from wireframes, it feeds usability testing and grows into high-fidelity prototypes as ideas hold up.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Nielsen Norman Group, a trusted source for UX research and design: https://www.nngroup.com/",
      "Hand-Off Deliverables Map": [
        {
