      ],
      "Deliverable Description": "UI development specifications are the detailed notes that tell developers exactly how a design should be built: sizes, spacing, colors, and behavior. They translate a design into build-ready instructions.",
      "Why Is This Deliverable Important?": "Clear specs prevent guesswork and mismatches between what was designed and what gets built, saving rounds of back-and-forth.",
      "How Does This Deliverable Relate to Other Deliverables?": "Created in Implement from high-fidelity prototypes, they pair with design annotations and the design system to guide developers.",
