      "Deliverable Description": "A microservices architecture builds a product out of small, independent services that each do one job and talk to each other. It is an alternative to one big, tightly linked system.",
      "Why Is This Deliverable Important?": "Splitting a system this way lets teams build, update, and scale parts independently, which suits fast, parallel agile work.",
      "How Does This Deliverable Relate to Other Deliverables?": "Designed in Implement, it is a form of the system and technical architecture and shapes how developers build and deploy.",
