        }
      ],
      "Deliverable Description": "Sprint retro action items are the concrete changes a team commits to after reflecting on a sprint. They turn 'we should do better' into specific next steps.",
      "Why Is This Deliverable Important?": "They are how continuous improvement actually happens, so a team gets a little better each cycle instead of repeating mistakes.",
      "How Does This Deliverable Relate to Other Deliverables?": "Captured across all milestones during retrospectives, they build on the sprint's demo and shape how the next sprint runs.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Agile Coach, with guides on agile, Scrum, and Kanban: https://www.atlassian.com/agile",
      "Hand-Off Deliverables Map": [
