      "Deliverable Description": "Task-level scope defines exactly what is included in a single task or story. It draws the boundary around one small piece of work.",
      "Why Is This Deliverable Important?": "Clear boundaries at the task level keep work from creeping and help the team estimate and finish reliably.",
      "How Does This Deliverable Relate to Other Deliverables?": "Set in Requirements from writing requirements and acceptance criteria, it rolls up into the larger release-level scope.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Agile Coach, with guides on agile, Scrum, and Kanban: https://www.atlassian.com/agile"
    },
