      "Deliverable Description": "A sprint goal is the single most important outcome a team aims for in a sprint. It is the one-sentence point of the cycle.",
      "Why Is This Deliverable Important?": "A clear goal keeps a sprint focused, so the team can make smart trade-offs and know whether the sprint succeeded.",
