      "Deliverable Description": "Code is the written instructions that make a product actually run. It is the raw material developers build software from.",
      "Why Is This Deliverable Important?": "It is where designs and plans finally become a working product, so its quality shows up directly in how well things function.",
      "How Does This Deliverable Relate to Other Deliverables?": "Written in Implement, it is guided by requirements, prototypes, and specs, and it is supported by coding documentation and tests.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "MDN Web Docs, a trusted resource for building software: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn"
