      "Deliverable Description": "A content outline is a structured plan for what content will go where, before the writing begins. It is the skeleton a piece of content is built on.",
      "Why Is This Deliverable Important?": "Outlining first keeps content organized and complete, so writers are not staring at a blank page or missing key points.",
      "How Does This Deliverable Relate to Other Deliverables?": "Created in Implement from the content inventory, it guides the copywriting and microcopy that follow.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Nielsen Norman Group, a trusted source for UX research and design: https://www.nngroup.com/"
    },
