      "Deliverable Description": "A psychological safety plan is a deliberate approach to building an environment where people feel safe to speak up, take risks, and make mistakes. It puts intention behind a healthy team culture.",
      "Why Is This Deliverable Important?": "Research ties psychological safety to how well teams perform, so planning for it directly strengthens the whole team.",
      "How Does This Deliverable Relate to Other Deliverables?": "Created in Intake alongside working agreements, it supports the trust and openness the rest of the team's work depends on.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Team Playbook, practical plays for healthy teamwork: https://www.atlassian.com/team-playbook"
    },
