      "Deliverable Description": "A meeting agenda is a short plan for what a meeting will cover and aim to decide. It sets the purpose before people gather.",
      "Why Is This Deliverable Important?": "Agendas keep meetings focused and respectful of people's time, so gatherings actually accomplish something.",
      "How Does This Deliverable Relate to Other Deliverables?": "Used across all milestones when scheduling meetings, they support the project management work that keeps things moving.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Agile Coach, with guides on agile, Scrum, and Kanban: https://www.atlassian.com/agile"
